1
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:05,180
Miyata.

2
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,460
When was the last time you wore a kimono?

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:11,010
Hmm... I can't remember.

4
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:13,880
I never really had much of a
chance to wear one anyway.

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:18,470
You're at the age where you should own
a kimono of your own.

6
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,270
Yeah, yeah.

7
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:25,370
Do you two have a special occasion today?

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,040
We're having dinner with some friends.

9
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:31,810
In that case, a casual kimono
would be perfect for this season.

10
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:33,740
A casual kimono...

11
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,670
Shall I find the right size for you?

12
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:39,260
I don't need one.
Just get one for him.

13
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:40,830
Right away.

14
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:47,810
A kimono dress code.
That's a first for me.

15
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:50,840
Kyosuke-san is quite elegant, isn't he?

16
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:54,040
Hmm... It doesn't
really seem like his style.

17
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,430
You think so?

18
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:02,100
Doesn't he usually just talk about
wine, cheese,

19
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:07,080
and French dishes
with unpronounceable names?

20
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:08,980
True.

21
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:12,260
Thank you for waiting.

22
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:17,680
This is a shantung silk fabric
with a unique luster.

23
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:22,030
The elegant light green
will look refreshing in the summer.

24
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,500
Okay.

25
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,230
Isn't this a bit too flashy?

26
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:33,360
You won't know until you try it on.

27
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,070
Please let him try it on.

28
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:38,300
Certainly.

29
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:39,820
Right this way, please.

30
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:05,660
Well...

31
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,480
How does it look?

32
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,280
Just as I imagined.

33
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,010
You look really good in a kimono.

34
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,870
It's surprisingly comfortable.

35
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,000
It suits you perfectly.

36
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:36,040
I'll go get another obi sash.

37
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:37,320
Thank you.

38
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:43,330
I guess we have Kyosuke-san's
whim to thank for this.

39
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,080
You look amazing.

40
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:01,890
Thanks.

41
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:22,900
Love is Better the Second
Time Around season2 (Episode 3)

42
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,880
What a great vibe.

43
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,770
After visiting the shrine...

44
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:03,200
Wow, the weather is beautiful.

45
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:05,080
The breeze feels so nice.

46
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,530
So relaxing.

47
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:10,080
I could just take a nap.

48
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:12,370
Huh?

49
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:17,770
As a side dish for dinner.

50
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:21,260
What should we do? Let's just buy them all.

51
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,400
They look delicious.

52
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,550
You're buying too much.

53
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:30,159
Excuse me, can we try a sample of this?

54
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:32,020
- Thank you.
- Don't mind if I do.

55
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,350
I'll have some black beans, too.

56
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:43,640
So good.

57
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:53,810
That sound is great, too.

58
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:55,250
Yeah.

59
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:34,390
By the way, it's way too hot.

60
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,596
Want to buy a folding
fan while we're at it?

61
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:38,420
Sounds good. Very elegant.

62
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,999
There's a fan shop just ahead.

63
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Huh?

64
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,220
Takashi-san.

65
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,050
Rui...?

66
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:52,969
First-name basis...?

67
00:05:52,970 --> 00:05:55,419
You really startled me.

68
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:56,579
What a coincidence.

69
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:57,970
What are you doing here?

70
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:00,330
Just finished shopping and heading back.

71
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:05,570
I'm so glad I came to Jindaiji today.

72
00:06:07,930 --> 00:06:10,870
So, who is this?

73
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:15,970
My boyfriend.

74
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:18,860
That's the first time I've been
introduced as his boyfriend.

75
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:19,950
Wow.

76
00:06:20,290 --> 00:06:22,020
You guys make a great couple.

77
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:24,880
Nice to meet you. I'm Miyata.

78
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,690
What about you, Rui?

79
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:32,260
We're on a date, too.

80
00:06:33,210 --> 00:06:34,470
Hi, I'm Sho.

81
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,870
Nice to meet you.

82
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:39,830
Is this the guy you mentioned before...

83
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:42,230
Yep, my ex-boyfriend.

84
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:44,370
Another one?

85
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:50,090
I heard he was an older, handsome guy.
It's totally true.

86
00:06:50,490 --> 00:06:51,570
Thanks.

87
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:56,720
Oh, I know!
Want to go on a double date?

88
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:58,660
Huh?

89
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:01,680
The more, the merrier, right?

90
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:04,460
Plus, it's been a while
since I saw Takashi-san.

91
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,590
Well...

92
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,640
Rui.

93
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,500
Yeah?

94
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,240
Let's just keep it to the two of us today.

95
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,060
Aww...

96
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:21,520
I want to spend some alone time with you.

97
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:23,980
Fine.

98
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:25,870
I get it.

99
00:07:27,170 --> 00:07:29,129
See you next time, Takashi-san.

100
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:29,740
Yeah.

101
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:31,550
See you next time, Miyata-san.

102
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:52,050
Another ex-boyfriend?

103
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,400
What a string of coincidences.

104
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:59,100
Just how many exes do you have?

105
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,500
It's a secret.

106
00:08:07,730 --> 00:08:11,750
Don't they say keeping a little mystery
makes a relationship last longer?

107
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:16,330
Am I being too nosy?

108
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:22,080
Why am I suddenly caring about
the time we spent apart?

109
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,520
Am I really this petty?

110
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:29,170
Miyata.

111
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:31,060
Why are you so quiet today?

112
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:36,030
It's probably the heat.
My brain is melting.

113
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:41,580
The shop is just ahead.
Hang in there a little longer.

114
00:08:50,310 --> 00:08:51,310
Oh.

115
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,860
Found it, found it.

116
00:08:58,990 --> 00:09:02,970
This one would go
perfectly with your kimono.

117
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:07,310
Yeah, the color and
material are a great match.

118
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,500
Look.

119
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:12,270
I don't really know much about it,

120
00:09:13,430 --> 00:09:15,550
but it's definitely cooling.

121
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:24,190
We've added another
treasure to our collection.

122
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:25,230
We sure have.

123
00:09:25,230 --> 00:09:26,050
Thank you.

124
00:09:26,050 --> 00:09:27,050
I'm really happy.

125
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,309
It would've been nice to
get matching ones, though.

126
00:09:29,310 --> 00:09:30,520
Yeah.

127
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:32,649
Let's buy more next time.

128
00:09:32,650 --> 00:09:33,650
Yeah.

129
00:09:37,450 --> 00:09:41,050
Those two look really happy together.

130
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,330
Does it bother you?

131
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:46,210
Not at all.

132
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:51,090
As long as Rui is happy,
I'm happy for him.

133
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:56,070
Looks like he's completely moved on.

134
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:07,910
Did he use to act like
this with Senpai, too...?

135
00:10:11,610 --> 00:10:13,730
Senpai,
let's go this way instead.

136
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,149
There's a shop I've been
wanting to check out.

137
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:18,849
It's rare for you to
take the lead like this.

138
00:10:18,850 --> 00:10:19,870
Is it?

139
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:24,879
Don't you usually just say,
"Anywhere is fine"?

140
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:26,560
I have places I want to go sometimes, too.

141
00:10:26,830 --> 00:10:28,370
Just be a good boy and follow me.

142
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:29,880
Yes, sir.

143
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:33,710
The menu has so many options.

144
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:35,210
- It's hard to choose.
- Yeah.

145
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:37,880
Anmitsu sounds good.

146
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,550
They have shiratama, too.

147
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:42,030
Oh, and zenzai!

148
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:44,709
Should we just order everything?

149
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:45,710
No way.

150
00:10:46,550 --> 00:10:47,910
Shaved ice?

151
00:10:49,390 --> 00:10:51,150
Or anmitsu?

152
00:10:51,730 --> 00:10:53,680
Man, what should I get?

153
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:58,190
Huh?

154
00:10:58,610 --> 00:10:59,960
Takashi-san?

155
00:11:00,010 --> 00:11:02,410
Rui. We meet again.

156
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:08,910
When we walked past the shop earlier,
I strongly sensed Takashi-san's presence.

157
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,470
And here you are.

158
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,250
Superpowers?

159
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:17,550
Magic?

160
00:11:17,790 --> 00:11:18,949
Please take a seat inside.

161
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:19,950
Okay.

162
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:23,180
Are you ready to order?

163
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:25,599
One mitsumame, please.

164
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,600
Certainly.

165
00:11:27,430 --> 00:11:31,470
Then... I'll have the
kiwi shiratama anmitsu.

166
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:32,510
Huh?

167
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:34,110
I'll have the same.

168
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:36,166
Are you sure you don't
want to look at the menu?

169
00:11:36,190 --> 00:11:38,110
It just sounded really good.

170
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:43,450
If Miyata-san ordered it,
it's got to be a winner.

171
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,080
Yeah.

172
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:51,750
Thank you for waiting.

173
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:53,210
Thank you.

174
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:55,610
Thanks.

175
00:11:55,611 --> 00:11:58,450
Here you go.
Enjoy your meal.

176
00:11:58,920 --> 00:11:59,710
Let's eat.

177
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:00,710
Let's eat.

178
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:15,120
The sweetness is just right.
It's delicious.

179
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,650
Yeah.

180
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,570
The kiwi is really good.

181
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:24,590
Yours looks pretty fancy.

182
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:26,580
It does.

183
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,490
Can I have one of your shiratama?

184
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:29,660
Sure.

185
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,500
Don't mind if I do.

186
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:34,540
Mmm, so good.

187
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,080
Hey, hey.

188
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,510
Let me have a bite, too.

189
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,180
Say "ah."

190
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,089
Mmm, so yummy.

191
00:12:46,090 --> 00:12:47,800
So cute.

192
00:12:48,390 --> 00:12:49,910
What else do you want?

193
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:51,600
A mandarin orange.

194
00:12:55,770 --> 00:12:56,770
Senpai.

195
00:12:56,980 --> 00:12:57,980
Hmm?

196
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:02,190
Ahh.

197
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,200
Ah?

198
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:08,740
Ah...

199
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:12,510
The food here
is as good as always.

200
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:13,920
Huh?

201
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:16,070
Isn't this your first time here?

202
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:17,280
No, I mean...

203
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:21,050
I meant it lives up to the reviews.
The quality is consistent...

204
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:22,340
Ah.

205
00:13:23,130 --> 00:13:24,130
So that's how it is.

206
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:26,260
But there's only one left.

207
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,720
You're impossible.

208
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:30,930
Say "ah."

209
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:34,490
Seriously, you're so stingy.

210
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:38,460
How can anyone
do this in front of others?

211
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:40,980
They're way too lovey-dovey.

212
00:13:46,410 --> 00:13:47,609
Thank you for the meal.

213
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:48,520
Thank you for the meal.

214
00:13:48,521 --> 00:13:49,990
Thank you for coming.

215
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,400
Rui, we'll be going now.

216
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,699
Huh?

217
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,960
Leaving so soon?

218
00:13:56,370 --> 00:13:57,830
I'm glad to see
you're doing well.

219
00:13:58,250 --> 00:13:59,460
You too, Takashi-san.

220
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,900
Ah, I'll DM you later.

221
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:03,340
Okay.

222
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:21,020
Did I buy too many sweets today?

223
00:14:30,490 --> 00:14:32,780
Mmm, so good.

224
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:36,950
Senpai.

225
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,080
Hmm?

226
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:43,850
Let me have a bite of that.

227
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:45,180
Sure.

228
00:14:47,510 --> 00:14:48,510
That's not what I meant.

229
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:57,180
Ahh.

230
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:11,570
Don't laugh.

231
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,050
What's wrong?

232
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:32,300
I've lost a bit of confidence.

233
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:42,410
Compared to a young, fresh guy like him.

234
00:15:46,110 --> 00:15:48,380
Even I think it's ridiculous.

235
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:52,460
By "young, fresh guy," do you mean Rui?

236
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:57,470
Don't tell me you're at it again?

237
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:00,249
I'm just jealous.

238
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,359
You really are something.

239
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,630
Please tell me.

240
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,630
Huh?

241
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:05,880
About Rui.

242
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:07,880
That's all in the past.

243
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,440
Don't try to brush me off.

244
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:15,030
Please try to understand how I feel,
constantly bumping into your exes.

245
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,480
Fair enough.

246
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,640
I get it.

247
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:32,250
Rui and I met four years ago.

248
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:40,760
I was out for a run.

249
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:59,060
Hello.

250
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:01,930
Hi.

251
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:05,020
Hey mister,
do you run around here often?

252
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:07,120
No, today's my first time.

253
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,769
I figured.

254
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:10,280
I've never seen you before.

255
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:14,530
This route is pretty
smooth and easy to run.

256
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:17,800
I'm Rui.

257
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:19,200
What about you, mister?

258
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,620
Iwanaga Takashi.

259
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,290
Nice to meet you.

260
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:25,620
Takashi-san.

261
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:31,069
Can I have a sip of that?

262
00:17:31,070 --> 00:17:33,480
Hmm? But I've already drank from it.

263
00:17:34,130 --> 00:17:37,360
Doesn't that make it taste even better?

264
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,790
Rui was a very charming kid.

265
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:55,090
He never hid his affection for me.

266
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,320
He always showed it without holding back.

267
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,390
So even when we broke up,

268
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:05,160
we didn't hide our true
feelings from each other.

269
00:18:08,250 --> 00:18:10,390
We ended the relationship very peacefully.

270
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:22,420
Anyway, I'm just not good at acting spoiled
or expressing my feelings.

271
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:30,910
But that's exactly what I
love about you, Miyata.

272
00:18:32,070 --> 00:18:34,040
So you don't need to change at all.

273
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,700
Senpai.

274
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:51,480
Want to do another "ah"?

275
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,670
No thanks.

276
00:19:00,478 --> 00:19:04,998
[He's looking at "book
design layout" options]

277
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:09,300
- Good work today.
- Good work.

278
00:19:10,310 --> 00:19:11,310
Miyata.

279
00:19:11,610 --> 00:19:14,540
How's the progress on
Teacher Iwanaga's project?

280
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,100
It's going smoothly.

281
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:20,420
I'm currently contacting a few designers
who might handle the book's binding.

282
00:19:21,300 --> 00:19:22,300
I see.

283
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:25,410
What's wrong?

284
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:28,540
Nothing.

285
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:33,640
I heard upper management is seriously
pushing for structural reform in the company.

286
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:37,520
Our department might
be getting a consultant too.

287
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:40,010
A consultant.

288
00:19:42,010 --> 00:19:47,070
I heard they'll ruthlessly cut
unprofitable projects and personnel.

289
00:19:50,810 --> 00:19:53,810
We both need to stay on our toes.

290
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:59,920
So, want to grab a drink tonight
and vent a little?

291
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,700
Sorry,
I already have plans today.

292
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:05,300
Ooh, going on a date?

293
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:07,160
Yes.

294
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:10,290
Well, sorry for bothering you then.

295
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:11,670
Let's do it another time.

296
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:12,700
Good work today.

297
00:20:12,710 --> 00:20:13,790
Yeah, good work.

298
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:30,100
Turn around.

299
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:33,020
- Right first, then left.
- Okay.

300
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:57,120
Can you hold onto that?

301
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:58,380
Yes.

302
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,360
I'm going to tighten it now.

303
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:32,780
Okay.

304
00:22:25,470 --> 00:22:28,760
- It should be right around here.
- Yeah.

305
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:32,470
It would be so much easier if he could just
send us his location on his phone.

306
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:35,600
Ah, Kyosuke-san.

307
00:22:38,850 --> 00:22:40,190
Hi.

308
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:45,610
Thanks for inviting us.

309
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,466
- Long time no see.
- I'm the one who should be thanking you.

310
00:22:47,490 --> 00:22:51,780
Not at all. Thank you for
indulging my selfishness.

311
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:56,209
It's not a houseboat.

312
00:22:56,210 --> 00:22:57,400
It's a Yakatabune.

313
00:22:58,120 --> 00:22:59,559
Is it a Yakatabune?

314
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:00,560
Yakatabune.

315
00:23:00,561 --> 00:23:02,219
- Yakatabune.
- Yakatabune.

316
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:03,550
So strict.

317
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:11,349
Are we the only ones on the boat today?

318
00:23:11,350 --> 00:23:12,350
No.

319
00:23:12,470 --> 00:23:13,970
There's one more person.

320
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,720
This is...

321
00:23:16,810 --> 00:23:17,980
Hello.

322
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:19,230
Takashi-san.

323
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:21,560
Miyata-san.

324
00:23:30,740 --> 00:23:34,119
(Next Episode Preview) I'm the most
important person to you, right, Senpai?

325
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:38,500
Do you still not understand
how crazy I am about you?

326
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:41,960
I can't imagine it at all.

327
00:23:42,250 --> 00:23:43,250
So innocent.

328
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:44,719
Are you making fun of me?

329
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:46,939
Aren't those two
standing a little too close?

330
00:23:46,940 --> 00:23:48,879
I don't really mind.

331
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:51,549
It seems you're the only man
who's ever dumped Takashi.

332
00:23:51,550 --> 00:23:52,980
It's a promise.

333
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,560
Why would you say something like that?

334
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:59,730
This is what you call
being jealous of the past.
